<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vivarais</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Vivarais is a historical region of south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, west of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhone">Rhône</a>, named after its episcopal city of Viviers and largely corresponding to the modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ardeche">Ardèche</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a>. It took over the territory of the Gallic Helvii, belonged to the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arles">Arles</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> and passed to the French crown in the late 13th and early 14th centuries.</p></div>
